# Wire builds — both services, one session

Shared architecture decisions (applying the playbook + your captures): **extraction happens in the MAIN world, targeted-only** — the relay never carries raw responses, so the classifier telemetry we saw in Gemini's record structurally cannot reach storage. Both injectors **buffer until the isolated world signals ready** (the first batch fetch can fire before the content script registers its listener). Z.ai round-matching is **exact** — the DOM `#message-<uuid>` ids are the wire message uuids (confirmed in both captures), so no fuzzy matching. Gemini filename lookup is keyed by **lh3 URL path token** (split at `=`), never by filename — your capture proved duplicates (`alien.prime.jpg` ×2, different URLs). Thinking backfill on Gemini rides the `r_→rc_` mapping from the id triples (works for turns with citations; broader linkage deferred — noted at the end).

